In <303sv4INNaej@duncan.cs.utk.edu> hzhou@cs.utk.edu (Honbo Zhou) writes:
>I would like to get pointers on where I could find documents
>about OSF DCE's data format conversion facility. Thanks.

DCE doesn't have a generic data format conversion facility.

Do you mean the data representation that is sent "over the wire" for RPC's?
(I.e., what the DCE equivalent is to Sun's ONC XDR?)

If so, then:
	DCE NDR, the network data representation, is derived from (and
	compatible with) the NDR used by Apollo's RPC system, NCS.  You
	can get technical specs from the book Network Computing Architecture,
	Zahn, et al ISBN 0-13-611674-4, by Prentice-Hall.

	The DCE RPC AES (a standards-type document for DCE RPC) also
	defines the data format.  It is available from Prentice-Hall
	ISBN 0-13-043688-7.  It is also available from X/Open.


