The Distributed Management Environment is a set of technologies for managing
distributed systems and consists of three major components:

 1. Distributed services (e.g., event notification, software distribution,
    software licensing, etc.). It was made available by OSF last year and
    is being licensed by some vendors (don't know who).

 2. Network Management Option (CMIP and SNMP management application framework).
    The telecom industry is very interested in this. OSF made it available
    earlier this year and, again, it's being licensed by various vendors.

 3. Network Management Framework (CORBA management application framework).
    OSF is working with vendors (e.g., HP, IBM, Digital, NEC) on CORBA
    over DCE interoperability and a submission to OMG for CORBA 2.0. OSF
    has made no announcement about NMF availability (it's possible that
    this technology may not emerge under the DME project but under some
    new distributed systems management effort in OSF using the new
    OSF project model).

For more information, contact OSF Direct at direct@osf.org or +1 617 621-7300.

