>I know Isis (but hav'nt a contact to the company), but I don't know, if
>Isis exist for AIX
>and I know that IBM have a Pthreads implementation. But we must be sure
>that the sources we have to implement with DCE Threads are portable.

DCE threads are just POSIX threads, or close enough as to make no difference.
I believe they are specified in POSIX 1003.4, Real Time Extensions.  If you
code to the OSF Application Development Guide/Reference, you should be fine
from a portability standpoint.  The pthread_ routines in section one of
the DCE reference manual are what you want.  Our code using those routines
runs fine on VMS, OSF/1 and HP/UX, so it's pretty portable stuff.

- Brad
